Package: rotationGWAS
Type: Package
Title: Rotation for Two-Stage Genome-Wide Association Analysis
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yawar", "Habib", email = "habib.yawr.10@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Hans-Peter", "Piepho", role = "aut"))
Description: Second-stage genome-wide association analysis of adjusted means from
    an unbalanced field trial, with the full variance-covariance matrix of the
    means carried forward by the rotation of Piepho et al. (2012). Given the
    adjusted means, their variance-covariance matrix, a relationship matrix,
    covariates and marker dosages, the package reports the marker-specific
    efficiency of inverse-variance and unweighted analysis before the genome
    scan, rotates every input with the same matrix, runs the P3D genome scan,
    tests the residual variance of the rotated model against one, and refits
    chosen markers with the residual variance fixed at one, and extends the
    model by an effect independent across accessions when the test finds the
    residual variance above one. The package starts after the first-stage
    analysis of the field trial; the vignette shows that first stage on the
    synthetic rolling-panel trials shipped with the package.
